  architecture guard: the DIAS runtime has no policy engine
    ✔ the deployed contracts never load the retained rule engine or disagreement guard
    ✔ the chaincode package excludes every retained policy-engine module
    ✔ runtime modules stay inside the package and never reach the offline oracle or guard
    ✔ loads the DIAS modules for verified requests, authorization, and lifecycle
    ✔ loads only the recommendation commitment, never a model, parser, prompt or registration

  rank ladder
    ✔ orders each department from low to high
    ✔ gives every role in every department a rank
    ✔ never compares ranks across departments

  authority resolution
    ✔ makes the highest-ranked officer at a station its head
    ✔ makes the highest-ranked officer in a district its head
    ✔ keeps departments separate
    ✔ routes a request to the station head when that head has the clearance
    ✔ routes past a station head who lacks the clearance, up to the district head
    ✔ skips the station tier for a requester with no station
    ✔ never routes a request to the requester themselves
    ✔ returns nothing when no authority in reach holds the clearance

  canonical ledger state
    the serializer is independent of insertion order
      ✔ produces identical bytes for the same content inserted in any order
      ✔ survives the spread that caused the divergence
      ✔ canonicalises nested objects and preserves array order
      ✔ still distinguishes different content
      ✔ refuses anything that is not a JSON object
      ✔ writes the canonical bytes through putJson
    no contract may bypass the serializer
      ✔ accessContract.js writes JSON state only through putJson
      ✔ accessContract.js never serialises STATE with JSON.stringify
      ✔ accessContract.js builds no event payload from spread state
      ✔ auditContract.js writes JSON state only through putJson
      ✔ auditContract.js never serialises STATE with JSON.stringify
      ✔ auditContract.js builds no event payload from spread state
      ✔ governanceContract.js writes JSON state only through putJson
      ✔ governanceContract.js never serialises STATE with JSON.stringify
      ✔ governanceContract.js builds no event payload from spread state
      ✔ recordContract.js writes JSON state only through putJson
      ✔ recordContract.js never serialises STATE with JSON.stringify
      ✔ recordContract.js builds no event payload from spread state
      ✔ userContract.js writes JSON state only through putJson
      ✔ userContract.js never serialises STATE with JSON.stringify
      ✔ userContract.js builds no event payload from spread state
      ✔ every contract imports the shared writer

  commitment hashing (dias-commitment-hash-v1)
    ✔ declares its format and the six domains of the design
    canonical JSON
      ✔ serializes {"b":2,"a":1}
      ✔ serializes {"outer":{"z":1,"a":[3,1,2]},"top":true}
      ✔ serializes {"é":1,"z":2,"A":3,"€":4}
      ✔ serializes {"ﬁ":1,"😀":2} (keys sort by UTF-16 code units (0xD83D < 0xFB01), not by code point)
      ✔ serializes {"string":"€$\u000f\nA'B\"\\\\\"/","literals":[null,true,false]} (RFC 8785 section 3.2.2.2 string example)
      ✔ serializes [0,-1,9007199254740991,-9007199254740991]
      ✔ serializes {}
      ✔ serializes []
      ✔ is independent of insertion order at every depth
      ✔ rejects non-integer number
      ✔ rejects unsafe integer
      ✔ rejects nested non-integer number
      ✔ rejects values JSON cannot represent exactly
      ✔ rejects strings with an unpaired surrogate anywhere, including keys
    domain-separated digests
      ✔ hashes note text "hello" to the shell reference
      ✔ hashes justification text "hello" to the shell reference
      ✔ hashes note text "" to the shell reference
      ✔ hashes justification text "café €" to the shell reference
      ✔ hashes canonical context JSON to the shell reference
      ✔ gives the same text different digests in different domains
      ✔ hashes text exactly: no trimming and no Unicode normalization
      ✔ detects any change to structured content
      ✔ refuses an unknown domain and non-string text
    digest format
      ✔ accepts exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters
      ✔ names the field when a digest is malformed

  DIAS access workflow safeguards
    request submission
      ✔ commits the structured action and purpose and keeps identity out of the verified context
      ✔ commits the justification only as its digest (h_J)
      ✔ refuses a request without a well-formed justification digest
      ✔ refuses the retired v2 emergencyFlag input instead of reading it as a fact
      ✔ rejects invalid request fields
      ✔ binds the request to the certificate-matched UserProfile
    auditor decision stage
      ✔ allows only AuditMSP district heads and takes the recommendation from the commitment
      ✔ prevents a requester from deciding their own request
      ✔ rejects a decision when governed facts changed after the request
      ✔ bounds revocation reasons and identifiers
    read access
      ✔ limits a request to its requester and district heads
      ✔ shows district heads the pending queue with the committed request and its commitment
      ✔ lets district heads query authorizations and their history
      ✔ limits access decisions to their subject and district heads

  DIAS access workflow
    request log
      ✔ records who asked for which record and waits for the auditor
      ✔ commits digests and the recommendation value, but never free text
    decision log: auditor FORCE_ALLOW that agreed with an LLM ALLOW
      ✔ grants access, records AGREED, and creates no dynamic authorization
    decision log: auditor FORCE_DENY that agreed with an LLM DENY
      ✔ denies access without creating a dynamic authorization
    decision log: auditor FORCE_ALLOW that did not agree with an LLM DENY
      ✔ grants access and creates an exact-record dynamic authorization
    decision log: auditor FORCE_DENY that did not agree with an LLM ALLOW
      ✔ denies access, records NOT_AGREED, and creates no dynamic authorization
    decision log: no LLM recommendation
      ✔ lets the auditor decide and never creates a dynamic authorization
    decision log, as a reviewer reads it
      ✔ lets a reviewer read who asked for what and what was decided
      ✔ shows an automatic grant as decided by its dynamic authorization
      ✔ returns the newest entries first and refuses an out-of-range limit
    reuse of an active dynamic authorization
      ✔ grants a repeat request with the auditor recorded as skipped
    no broad reuse
      ✔ does not reuse the authorization for another record, action, purpose, or user
      ✔ does not reuse the authorization after a governed fact changes
    explicit revocation
      ✔ requires a district head and a reason, records the change, and stops reuse
      ✔ creates a new generation when a revoked scope is approved again
    expiry
      ✔ stops reuse after validUntilUtc and records the expiry transition
      ✔ rejects an expiry when no dynamic authorization is created
    FORCE_DENY
      ✔ never revokes other authorizations

  DIAS auditor authority (plan step 3)
    credential status
      ✔ rejects a decision by an auditor whose ledger profile is suspended
      ✔ rejects a decision by an auditor whose ledger profile is revoked
      ✔ rejects a decision signed with a certificate whose credential is not active
      ✔ rejects a district head with no ledger profile
      ✔ rejects a certificate that does not match the auditor profile
    district and clearance
      ✔ rejects a district head of another district
      ✔ rejects a district head without clearance for the record
      ✔ accepts an active district head of the record district with clearance
      ✔ still refuses a decision on the auditor own request
    revocation
      ✔ requires the same active, in-district authority

  AuditContract
    GetRequestAuditTrail
      ✔ reconstructs a reviewed request that created a dynamic authorization
      ✔ reconstructs a reused authorization with the auditor skipped, and a later revocation
      ✔ lets the requester read their own trail and refuses other identities
    record-level trail and verification
      ✔ lists the DIAS requests and release grants for a record
      ✔ confirms a matching payload hash and flags a tampered one
    direct-ledger access events
      ✔ derives the actor from the signing identity and stores the event
      ✔ allows reviewers to query and rejects ordinary departments
      ✔ rejects malformed event fields and limits

  DIAS dynamic authorization scope
    ✔ is exact: user, record, case, action, and purpose each change the scope

  DIAS dynamic authorization creation
    ✔ records the originating request, auditor decision, LLM agreement, scope, and conditions
    ✔ is refused unless the auditor FORCE_ALLOW did not agree with an LLM DENY
    ✔ validates identifiers, auditor identity, and expiry
    ✔ increments the generation when it replaces an earlier authorization

  DIAS dynamic authorization matching
    ✔ matches only an active, unexpired authorization with unchanged conditions
    ✔ does not match when no authorization or a different scope is stored
    ✔ reports revoked, superseded, expired, and changed-condition misses

  DIAS dynamic authorization state transitions
    ✔ revokes without mutating the previous state
    ✔ expires and supersedes with an incremented state version

  DIAS dynamic authorization policy binding (v3)
    ✔ stores the policy it is issued under and refuses to be issued without one
    ✔ reports POLICY_CHANGED, not a match, under another active policy
    ✔ never matches an authorization of an older schema

  DIAS lifecycle events
    ✔ writes ordered, transaction-bound events under the request ID
    ✔ keeps request event streams isolated even when IDs share a prefix
    ✔ stores authorization events in their own key space
    ✔ emits one chaincode event naming every committed stage

  DIAS auditor note commitment (plan step 11)
    ✔ returns the committed decision with its note digest in the auditor review, for read-back
    ✔ rejects a malformed note digest before reading anything
    a note digest is required
      ✔ rejects FORCE_ALLOW over a committed DENY (NOT_AGREED) without one, writing nothing
      ✔ rejects FORCE_DENY over a committed ALLOW (NOT_AGREED) without one, writing nothing
      ✔ rejects a committed failure status (NO_RECOMMENDATION) without one, writing nothing
      ✔ rejects no commitment at all (NO_RECOMMENDATION) without one, writing nothing
      ✔ accepts the same decision once the digest is supplied, and records it
    an agreeing decision
      ✔ needs no note, and records that none was given
      ✔ may carry a note digest, which is recorded

  DIAS policy governance and binding (plan step 8)
    policy registry
      ✔ activates the seeded policy and reports it as active
      ✔ needs a different district head to activate than the one who registered
      ✔ never re-activates a retired version and refuses duplicates and malformed input
      ✔ accepts registration and activation only from active AuditMSP district heads
      ✔ refuses every request while no policy is active
    binding
      ✔ binds a request, its decision, outcome and authorization to the active policy
      ✔ rejects a decision once another policy is active, then lets the request be expired
      ✔ stops reusing an authorization after a policy change, without changing its status
      ✔ reissues the authorization under the new policy as a new generation
    release after a policy change
      ✔ refuses to release a reviewed grant issued under a retired policy
      ✔ refuses to release a reused grant issued under a retired policy
    records without a policy binding
      ✔ never reuses an authorization or releases a grant that carries no policy

  policy digest of the repository policy
    ✔ matches the binding the test world activates, so tests use the real policy identity

  DIAS privacy controls (plan step 13)
    record history
      ✔ is readable by a reviewer and by the owning station
      ✔ is refused for another station, another organization, and a reviewer organization without the role
      ✔ is refused for an owning-station member whose credential is not active
      ✔ refuses a record that does not exist instead of returning an empty history
    evidence list and custody chain
      ✔ is readable by a reviewer and by same-district police, forensics, prosecution and court
      ✔ is refused outside the record's district
      ✔ is refused for a same-district member whose credential is not active
      ✔ lets a seal-authority reviewer of another district read, because reviewers are not district-bound
    decision log
      ✔ is full for reviewers
      ✔ is redacted for everyone else, the requester included
    the recommendation, for the requester, follows the auditor decision
      ✔ is withheld from the requester until an auditor has decided
      ✔ is always visible to the auditors and reviewers
      ✔ is shown to the requester once the auditor has decided, whatever the decision
      ✔ stays withheld from the requester when the request ends without a decision

  DIAS pre-review recommendation commitment (plan steps 10 and 12)
    signer registry
      ✔ registers an Ed25519 key under the digest of its public key
      ✔ refuses duplicates, other key types, malformed keys and non-auditors
      ✔ stops accepting commitments signed by a revoked key, and revocation needs a reason
    acceptance
      ✔ commits a signed recommendation before review, bound to the request
      ✔ treats an identical resubmission as a safe retry that writes nothing
      ✔ rejects a different commitment for the same request without writing
      ✔ keeps every specific generation failure status
    rejection
      ✔ rejects commitments whose bindings do not match the request
      ✔ rejects inconsistent or malformed content
      ✔ rejects a commitment changed after signing, or signed by an unregistered key
      ✔ rejects a valid commitment replayed onto another request
      ✔ rejects a commitment after the deadline, a policy change, or a decision
    agreement derived from the commitment (paper Eq. 3)
      ✔ ALLOW + FORCE_ALLOW -> AGREED
      ✔ ALLOW + FORCE_DENY -> NOT_AGREED
      ✔ DENY + FORCE_ALLOW -> NOT_AGREED, authorization created
      ✔ DENY + FORCE_DENY -> AGREED
      ✔ a committed UNAVAILABLE -> NO_RECOMMENDATION with the specific status
      ✔ a committed INVALID_OUTPUT -> NO_RECOMMENDATION with the specific status
      ✔ a committed POLICY_CONTEXT_UNAVAILABLE -> NO_RECOMMENDATION with the specific status
      ✔ a committed CONTEXT_OVERFLOW -> NO_RECOMMENDATION with the specific status
      ✔ no commitment at all -> NO_RECOMMENDATION recorded as NOT_COMMITTED
      ✔ takes no recommendation from the caller: the third argument is the note digest

